commit fe6b85bfa029d37fe1b6e149b523f950bd9869d1
Author: Marius Momeu <marius.momeu@berkeley.edu>
Date:   Fri Nov 13 19:12:33 2026 +0000

    opt.c: wrap 3 items (wave-186/batch-2/run-1)

    st::cli_opt_spec
    st::cli_opt
    st::cli_opt_parser

    The type route of opt.c's waves 187 and 188, folded onto wave 186: opt.h's
    structs keep their C layouts behind a safe API in opt.rs's ffi_import, as the
    CLI's remaining C builds and reads them in place until their port/layout.
    define_ctype! mints Spec<'p>, Opt<'p> and Parser<'p>, invariant in the borrow
    of what they point at, all CZeroable and neither Send nor Sync; each typedef
    shares its struct's anchor. A spec's type and void *value are one Target<'p>,
    written together, whose variables are Cells (switches share them), an
    Arg<'p> per C-string argument, and an ArgsSlot for &args[idx]. SpecTable is a
    spec run up to its zeroed end. Parser::new wraps cli_opt_parser_init, its init
    constructor. Kind's and Status's integer conversions lose their dead_code
    expectations. The git2 allowlist gains the three structs and cli_opt_parse,
    and the bindings are regenerated. The ownership store gains the 13 pointer
    fields' findings and cli_opt_parser_init's init role. 17 unit_pub, 6 ub_safe,
    5 equiv tests and 7 compile-fail doctests. Proposals:
    type-erased-field-tagged-by-a-sibling (binding-types, crustify 755ff2c on its
    evolution branch) and compile-fail-doctest-codes-unchecked-on-stable (testing).

    Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>

